c/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/team-impl-log.md:81:  - spec-deviation ruling: approved by impl-lead (retryable failure reasons formatted 'provider_failure: <kind>: <message>' to satisfy both TC-2.3 exhaustion shape and immutable Epic 02 verbatim-copy contract; terminal kinds stay kind-led; Story 4 TC-3.1 must consume same format)\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/team-impl-log.md:80:- Story-lead: run-001. Implementor evidence: artifacts/03-view-contents-report/003-implementor.json. Verifier: initial BLOCK (SV-03-001 public-contract tension), final PASS with SV-03-001 fixed after impl-lead ruling-011.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/team-impl-log.md:82:- Findings dispositions: SV-03-001 fixed.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/test-plan.md:76:- exhaustion leg: all-whitespace script → form `failed`, reason `provider_failure`, last error names `empty_output`\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/test-plan.md:83:- `network` to exhaustion → `failed`, `provider_failure`, `metadata.lastError` preserved\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/epic.md:126:- **AC-3.2**: Classified failures drive Epic 02's machinery unchanged: retryable failures back off and retry within budget; exhaustion → `failed` with reason `provider_failure`, attempts and last error in form metadata; terminal failures → `failed` on first attempt, no further calls for that item.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/epic.md:131:- **TC-3.1** (AC-3.1, AC-3.2): Scripted failures — function returns `rate_limit` twice then succeeds → form `ready`, attempts recorded; function returns `auth` → form `failed` immediately, exactly one call made, stable reason; exhaust a `network`-failing item → `failed`, `provider_failure`, last error preserved.\npackages/lhc/src/inference/adapter.ts:43:// `provider_failure` — the code Epic 02 has always landed on exhausted forms\npackages/lhc/src/inference/adapter.ts:53:    reason: retryable ? `provider_failure: ${detail}` : detail,\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts.md:47:  - all-whitespace script exhausts budget; form lands `failed` with reason `provider_failure` and last error naming `empty_output`\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/04-failure-classification.md:25:- **AC-3.2**: Classified failures drive Epic 02's machinery unchanged: retryable failures back off and retry within budget; exhaustion → `failed` with reason `provider_failure`, attempts and last error in form metadata; terminal failures → `failed` on first attempt, no further calls for that item.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/04-failure-classification.md:34:  - `network` failures exhaust; form lands `failed`, reason `provider_failure`, and `metadata.lastError` is preserved\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/04-failure-classification.md:131:| retryable exhausted | existing failed-form path | `failed`, reason `provider_failure`, attempts and last error preserved |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/tech-design.md:291:Construction errors are `TypeError`s naming the violated rule (existing contract): `\"createSdk config: exactly one of provider or inference\"`, `\"inference.assignments missing kind chunk_summary_brief\"`, `\"inference.assignments.smoothed_prompt.prompt names unknown template 'smoothing-v2'\"`, `\"view.visibility.maxTokens must be > targetTokens\"`. Operating failures never throw: they are `ProviderResult` failures with `reason` = the failure kind, flowing into form state via the unchanged Epic 02 paths (`failed` with reason `provider_failure` at exhaustion, terminal kinds immediately).\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/quick-fix/streams/001-quick-fix.stdout.log:23:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01Tu2CqBiuYgPMiKToen3y1z\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"1\\t// The real provider (DD-2): createInferenceProvider returns the same\\n2\\t// DerivationProvider interface the deterministic provider implements, so\\n3\\t// createSdk and everything below it see a provider, full stop. Every\\n4\\t// operation is the same five-step pipeline (Flow 2): bound the input where\\n5\\t// DD-7 applies, render the kind's prompt template into single-turn messages,\\n6\\t// call the host ModelCall with the kind's assignment, reject empty or\\n7\\t// whitespace-only text as empty_output (AC-2.4), and return the shaped text\\n8\\t// with config-known provenance (AC-2.5). The adapter never parses model text\\n9\\t// for outcomes, receipts, or any mechanical fact — those stay\\n10\\t// handler-authored from the record. The safeCall timeout race (DD-6)\\n11\\t// supersedes the inline thrown-exception containment in the classification\\n12\\t// story.\\n13\\timport type {\\n14\\t  DerivationProvider,\\n15\\t  FormKind,\\n16\\t  ProviderResult,\\n17\\t} from \\\"../shared/derivation.js\\\";\\n18\\timport { FAILURE_CLASSIFICATION } from \\\"./classify.js\\\";\\n19\\timport { PROMPT_REGISTRY, type PromptTemplate } from \\\"./prompts/index.js\\\";\\n20\\timport type {\\n21\\t  ModelCallFailureKind,\\n22\\t  ModelCallResult,\\n23\\t  ResolvedInferenceConfig,\\n24\\t} from \\\"./types.js\\\";\\n25\\t\\n26\\t// DD-7: a pathological tool result must not blow a small-context model.\\n27\\t// Content over the bound keeps its head and tail around a marker, and the\\n28\\t// bounded whole stays within maxInputChars; bounding happens before prompt\\n29\\t// rendering, so the dropped middle never crosses the boundary.\\n30\\tfunction boundContent(content: string, maxInputChars: number): string {\\n31\\t  if (content.length <= maxInputChars) return content;\\n32\\t  const marker = `\\\\n\\\\n[... truncated: tool result was ${String(content.length)} chars; head and tail retained ...]\\\\n\\\\n`;\\n33\\t  const keep = Math.max(0, maxInputChars - marker.length);\\n34\\t  const head = Math.ceil(keep / 2);\\n35\\t  const tail = keep - head;\\n36\\t  return content.slice(0, head) + marker + (tail > 0 ? content.slice(content.length - tail) : \\\"\\\");\\n37\\t}\\n38\\t\\n39\\t// Failure mapping (DD-3): the queue consumes `retryable` exactly as it always\\n40\\t// has, and the reason string is machine-readable by the established\\n41\\t// code-before-first-colon convention. Retryable failures lead with\\n42\\t// `provider_failure` — the code Epic 02 has always landed on exhausted forms\\n43\\t// (the queue copies the provider's reason verbatim at exhaustion, AC-3.2) —\\n44\\t// with the failure kind named next; terminal kinds lead with the kind itself\\n45\\t// and land failed immediately.\\n46\\tfunction classifiedFailure(kind: ModelCallFailureKind, message: string): ProviderResult {\\n47\\t  const { retryable } = FAILURE_CLASSIFICATION[kind];\\n48\\t  const detail = message === \\\"\\\" ? kind : `${kind}: ${message}`;\\n49\\t  return {\\n50\\t    ok: false,\\n51\\t    retryable,\\n52\\t    reason: retryable ? `provider_failure: ${detail}` : detail,\\n53\\t  };\\n54\\t}\\n55\\t\\n56\\texport function createInferenceProvider(config: ResolvedInferenceConfig): DerivationProvider {\\n57\\t  const callKind = async (kind: FormKind, input: unknown): Promise<ProviderResult> => {\\n58\\t    const assignment = config.assignments[kind];\\n59\\t    // Construction validated the name (AC-1.3); a miss here is registry\\n60\\t    // drift after construction and is terminal, never retried into.\\n61\\t    const template = PROMPT_REGISTRY[assignment.prompt] as PromptTemplate<unknown> | undefined;\\n62\\t    if (template === undefined) {\\n63\\t      return classifiedFailure(\\n64\\t        \\\"invalid_request\\\",\\n65\\t        `prompt template \\\"${assignment.prompt}\\\" not in registry`,\\n66\\t      );\\n67\\t    }\\n68\\t    const messages = template.render(input);\\n69\\t    let result: ModelCallResult;\\n70\\t    try {\\n71\\t      result = await config.call({\\n72\\t        provider: assignment.provider,\\n73\\t        model: assignment.model,\\n74\\t        messages,\\n75\\t      });\\n76\\t    } catch (cause) {\\n77\\t      // Thrown host exceptions classify as `other` (AC-3.3); the structured\\n78\\t      // safeCall wrapper (timeout race, DD-6) supersedes this containment in\\n79\\t      // the classification story.\\n80\\t      result = { ok: false, kind: \\\"other\\\", message: String(cause) };\\n81\\t    }\\n82\\t    if (!result.ok) {\\n83\\t      return classifiedFailure(result.kind, result.message);\\n84\\t    }\\n85\\t    // Shaping: surrounding whitespace never becomes form content — and a\\n86\\t    // model that returned nothing but whitespace has not produced a\\n87\\t    // derivation (AC-2.4): a classified retryable failure, never a ready\\n88\\t    // form. `empty_output` is adapter-generated; hosts never return it.\\n89\\t    const text = result.text.trim();\\n90\\t    if (text === \\\"\\\") {\\n91\\t      return classifiedFailure(\\\"empty_output\\\", \\\"model returned empty or whitespace-only text\\\");\\n92\\t    }\\n93\\t    // Provenance is the assignment's three config-known strings, copied —\\n94\\t    // never authored from model output (DD-4).\\n95\\t    return {\\n96\\t      ok: true,\\n97\\t      text,\\n98\\t      provenance: {\\n99\\t        provider: assignment.provider,\\n100\\t        model: assignment.model,\\n101\\t        prompt: assignment.prompt,\\n102\\t      },\\n103\\t    };\\n104\\t  };\\n105\\t\\n106\\t  return {\\n107\\t    smoothPrompt: (i) => callKind(\\\"smoothed_prompt\\\", i),\\n108\\t    summarizeToolCall: (i) => callKind(\\\"tool_call_summary\\\", i),\\n109\\t    summarizeToolResult: (i) =>\\n110\\t      callKind(\\\"tool_result_summary\\\", {\\n111\\t        toolName: i.toolName,\\n112\\t        content: boundContent(i.content, config.maxInputChars),\\n113\\t      }),\\n114\\t    composeTurnRendering: (i) => callKind(\\\"turn_rendering\\\", i),\\n115\\t    projectLowerBand: (i) => callKind(\\\"lower_band_projection\\\", i),\\n116\\t    summarizeChunkDetailed: (i) => callKind(\\\"chunk_summary_detailed\\\", i),\\n117\\t    summarizeChunkBrief: (i) => callKind(\\\"chunk_summary_brief\\\", i),\\n118\\t  };\\n119\\t}\\n120\\t\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"7cef6c87-78e2-45ca-98c2-725c469882de\",\"uuid\":\"78a9f4bd-92b4-422a-810c-d388f30b99cb\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-12T22:44:44.634Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/src/inference/adapter.ts\",\"content\":\"// The real provider (DD-2): createInferenceProvider returns the same\\n// DerivationProvider interface the deterministic provider implements, so\\n// createSdk and everything below it see a provider, full stop. Every\\n// operation is the same five-step pipeline (Flow 2): bound the input where\\n// DD-7 applies, render the kind's prompt template into single-turn messages,\\n// call the host ModelCall with the kind's assignment, reject empty or\\n// whitespace-only text as empty_output (AC-2.4), and return the shaped text\\n// with config-known provenance (AC-2.5). The adapter never parses model text\\n// for outcomes, receipts, or any mechanical fact — those stay\\n// handler-authored from the record. The safeCall timeout race (DD-6)\\n// supersedes the inline thrown-exception containment in the classification\\n// story.\\nimport type {\\n  DerivationProvider,\\n  FormKind,\\n  ProviderResult,\\n} from \\\"../shared/derivation.js\\\";\\nimport { FAILURE_CLASSIFICATION } from \\\"./classify.js\\\";\\nimport { PROMPT_REGISTRY, type PromptTemplate } from \\\"./prompts/index.js\\\";\\nimport type {\\n  ModelCallFailureKind,\\n  ModelCallResult,\\n  ResolvedInferenceConfig,\\n} from \\\"./types.js\\\";\\n\\n// DD-7: a pathological tool result must not blow a small-context model.\\n// Content over the bound keeps its head and tail around a marker, and the\\n// bounded whole stays within maxInputChars; bounding happens before prompt\\n// rendering, so the dropped middle never crosses the boundary.\\nfunction boundContent(content: string, maxInputChars: number): string {\\n  if (content.length <= maxInputChars) return content;\\n  const marker = `\\\\n\\\\n[... truncated: tool result was ${String(content.length)} chars; head and tail retained ...]\\\\n\\\\n`;\\n  const keep = Math.max(0, maxInputChars - marker.length);\\n  const head = Math.ceil(keep / 2);\\n  const tail = keep - head;\\n  return content.slice(0, head) + marker + (tail > 0 ? content.slice(content.length - tail) : \\\"\\\");\\n}\\n\\n// Failure mapping (DD-3): the queue consumes `retryable` exactly as it always\\n// has, and the reason string is machine-readable by the established\\n// code-before-first-colon convention. Retryable failures lead with\\n// `provider_failure` — the code Epic 02 has always landed on exhausted forms\\n// (the queue copies the provider's reason verbatim at exhaustion, AC-3.2) —\\n// with the failure kind named next; terminal kinds lead with the kind itself\\n// and land failed immediately.\\nfunction classifiedFailure(kind: ModelCallFailureKind, message: string): ProviderResult {\\n  const { retryable } = FAILURE_CLASSIFICATION[kind];\\n  const detail = message === \\\"\\\" ? kind : `${kind}: ${message}`;\\n  return {\\n    ok: false,\\n    retryable,\\n    reason: retryable ? `provider_failure: ${detail}` : detail,\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nexport function createInferenceProvider(config: ResolvedInferenceConfig): DerivationProvider {\\n  const callKind = async (kind: FormKind, input: unknown): Promise<ProviderResult> => {\\n    const assignment = config.assignments[kind];\\n    // Construction validated the name (AC-1.3); a miss here is registry\\n    // drift after construction and is terminal, never retried into.\\n    const template = PROMPT_REGISTRY[assignment.prompt] as PromptTemplate<unknown> | undefined;\\n    if (template === undefined) {\\n      return classifiedFailure(\\n        \\\"invalid_request\\\",\\n        `prompt template \\\"${assignment.prompt}\\\" not in registry`,\\n      );\\n    }\\n    const messages = template.render(input);\\n    let result: ModelCallResult;\\n    try {\\n      result = await config.call({\\n        provider: assignment.provider,\\n        model: assignment.model,\\n        messages,\\n      });\\n    } catch (cause) {\\n      // Thrown host exceptions classify as `other` (AC-3.3); the structured\\n      // safeCall wrapper (timeout race, DD-6) supersedes this containment in\\n      // the classification story.\\n      result = { ok: false, kind: \\\"other\\\", message: String(cause) };\\n    }\\n    if (!result.ok) {\\n      return classifiedFailure(result.kind, result.message);\\n    }\\n    // Shaping: surrounding whitespace never becomes form content — and a\\n    // model that returned nothing but whitespace has not produced a\\n    // derivation (AC-2.4): a classified retryable failure, never a ready\\n    // form. `empty_output` is adapter-generated; hosts never return it.\\n    const text = result.text.trim();\\n    if (text === \\\"\\\") {\\n      return classifiedFailure(\\\"empty_output\\\", \\\"model returned empty or whitespace-only text\\\");\\n    }\\n    // Provenance is the assignment's three config-known strings, copied —\\n    // never authored from model output (DD-4).\\n    return {\\n      ok: true,\\n      text,\\n      provenance: {\\n        provider: assignment.provider,\\n        model: assignment.model,\\n        prompt: assignment.prompt,\\n      },\\n    };\\n  };\\n\\n  return {\\n    smoothPrompt: (i) => callKind(\\\"smoothed_prompt\\\", i),\\n    summarizeToolCall: (i) => callKind(\\\"tool_call_summary\\\", i),\\n    summarizeToolResult: (i) =>\\n      callKind(\\\"tool_result_summary\\\", {\\n        toolName: i.toolName,\\n        content: boundContent(i.content, config.maxInputChars),\\n      }),\\n    composeTurnRendering: (i) => callKind(\\\"turn_rendering\\\", i),\\n    projectLowerBand: (i) => callKind(\\\"lower_band_projection\\\", i),\\n    summarizeChunkDetailed: (i) => callKind(\\\"chunk_summary_detailed\\\", i),\\n    summarizeChunkBrief: (i) => callKind(\\\"chunk_summary_brief\\\", i),\\n  };\\n}\\n\",\"numLines\":120,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":120}}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/quick-fix/streams/001-quick-fix.stdout.log:248:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01Jo1TwencYXr3bbWNe3a18C\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"The file /Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/src/inference/adapter.ts has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"7cef6c87-78e2-45ca-98c2-725c469882de\",\"uuid\":\"9f8042a6-79f5-4eeb-8d5d-a24a6fc2259d\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-12T22:46:12.714Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/src/inference/adapter.ts\",\"oldString\":\"function boundContent(content: string, maxInputChars: number): string {\\n  if (content.length <= maxInputChars) return content;\\n  const marker = `\\\\n\\\\n[... truncated: tool result was ${String(content.length)} chars; head and tail retained ...]\\\\n\\\\n`;\\n  const keep = Math.max(0, maxInputChars - marker.length);\\n  const head = Math.ceil(keep / 2);\\n  const tail = keep - head;\\n  return content.slice(0, head) + marker + (tail > 0 ? content.slice(content.length - tail) : \\\"\\\");\\n}\",\"newString\":\"function boundContent(content: string, maxInputChars: number): string {\\n  if (content.length <= maxInputChars) return content;\\n  const marker = `\\\\n\\\\n[... truncated: tool result was ${String(content.length)} chars; head and tail retained ...]\\\\n\\\\n`;\\n  // The marker only earns its place 